  <content>
    <section class="practice" id="sect-00001">
      <note id="note-00001">
        <para id="para-00001">Access the <link url="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/2c2987f83130584132cad08b60ad0d3ba45a32b9">Desmos guide PDF</link> for tips on solving problems with the Desmos graphing calculator.</para></note>
      <para id="para-00002">Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson.</para>
      <list class="os-raise-noindent" list-type="enumerated" id="list-00001">
        <item>Enter the given data into Desmos, then calculate the regression approximation to determine the curve of best fit. <table class="unnumbered os-raise-skinnytable" id="table-00001">
            <tgroup cols="2">
              <tbody>
                <row>
                  <entry><emphasis><m:math><m:mrow><m:msub><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>1</m:mn></m:msub></m:mrow></m:math></emphasis>
                  </entry>
                  <entry><emphasis><m:math><m:mrow><m:msub><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mn>1</m:mn></m:msub></m:mrow></m:math></emphasis>
                  </entry>
                </row>
                <row>
                  <entry> 2 </entry>
                  <entry> 56 </entry>
                </row>
                <row>
                  <entry> 5 </entry>
                  <entry> 116 </entry>
                </row>
                <row>
                  <entry> 8 </entry>
                  <entry> 155 </entry>
                </row>
                <row>
                  <entry> 11 </entry>
                  <entry> 205 </entry>
                </row>
                <row>
                  <entry> 17 </entry>
                  <entry> 230 </entry>
                </row>
              </tbody>
            </tgroup>
          </table>
        </item>
      </list>
      <media alt="...">
        <iframe src="../../media/desmos/73a41d9f6d133fb73de34f9f4ccacd50756a4c9c.html" width="500" height="400"/>
      </media>
      <para id="para-00003">What is the equation for the curve of best fit that models the data?</para>
      <exercise id="_2bb7ca48-10c1-470e-8d66-afc1bebad136" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00001">
          <para id="para-00004">Multiple Choice:</para>
          <para id="para-00005"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>0.93</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>22.63</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>10.48</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para><para id="para-00006"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>0.69</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>24.83</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>8.07</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para><para id="para-00007"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>3.11</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>16.32</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>8.94</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para><para id="para-00008"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>0.7</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>35.93</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>8.19</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para></problem>
        <solution id="sol-00001">
          <para id="para-00009">Try again. Revisit activity 8.12.2.</para>
          <para id="para-00010">The correct answer is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>0.69</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>24.83</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>8.07</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <list class="os-raise-noindent" list-type="enumerated" id="list-00002">
        <item>Enter the given data into Desmos, then calculate the regression approximation to determine the curve of best fit. <table class="unnumbered os-raise-skinnytable" id="table-00002">
            <tgroup cols="2">
              <tbody>
                <row>
                  <entry><emphasis><m:math><m:mrow><m:msub><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>1</m:mn></m:msub></m:mrow></m:math></emphasis>
                  </entry>
                  <entry><emphasis><m:math><m:mrow><m:msub><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mn>1</m:mn></m:msub></m:mrow></m:math></emphasis>
                  </entry>
                </row>
                <row>
                  <entry> 3 </entry>
                  <entry> 105 </entry>
                </row>
                <row>
                  <entry> 9 </entry>
                  <entry> 250 </entry>
                </row>
                <row>
                  <entry> 14 </entry>
                  <entry> 349 </entry>
                </row>
                <row>
                  <entry> 23 </entry>
                  <entry> 400 </entry>
                </row>
                <row>
                  <entry> 37 </entry>
                  <entry> 258 </entry>
                </row>
              </tbody>
            </tgroup>
          </table>
        </item>
      </list>
      <media alt="...">
        <iframe src="../../media/desmos/73a41d9f6d133fb73de34f9f4ccacd50756a4c9c.html" width="500" height="400"/>
      </media>
      <para id="para-00011">What is the equation for the curve of best fit that models the data?</para>
      <exercise id="a6c9e4b8-a75e-4a58-9f4a-4e8de2a59766" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00002">
          <para id="para-00012">Multiple Choice:</para>
          <para id="para-00013"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>0.56</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>38.74</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>5.31</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para><para id="para-00014"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>2.31</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>24.711</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>3.25</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para><para id="para-00015"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>0.62</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>17.45</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>9.64</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para><para id="para-00016"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>0.74</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>34.32</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>7.44</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para></problem>
        <solution id="sol-00002">
          <para id="para-00017">Try again. Revisit activities 8.12.2.</para>
          <para id="para-00018">The correct answer is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>0.74</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>34.32</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>7.44</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <list class="os-raise-noindent" list-type="enumerated" id="list-00003">
        <item>Enter the given data into Desmos, then calculate the regression approximation to determine the curve of best fit. <table class="unnumbered os-raise-skinnytable" id="table-00003">
            <tgroup cols="2">
              <tbody>
                <row>
                  <entry><emphasis><m:math><m:mrow><m:msub><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>1</m:mn></m:msub></m:mrow></m:math></emphasis>
                  </entry>
                  <entry><emphasis><m:math><m:mrow><m:msub><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mn>1</m:mn></m:msub></m:mrow></m:math></emphasis>
                  </entry>
                </row>
                <row>
                  <entry> 0.2 </entry>
                  <entry> 6.5 </entry>
                </row>
                <row>
                  <entry> 0.35 </entry>
                  <entry> 6.74 </entry>
                </row>
                <row>
                  <entry> 0.66 </entry>
                  <entry> 6.31 </entry>
                </row>
                <row>
                  <entry> 1 </entry>
                  <entry> 4.95 </entry>
                </row>
                <row>
                  <entry> 1.5 </entry>
                  <entry> 1.2 </entry>
                </row>
              </tbody>
            </tgroup>
          </table>
        </item>
      </list>
      <media alt="...">
        <iframe src="../../media/desmos/73a41d9f6d133fb73de34f9f4ccacd50756a4c9c.html" width="500" height="400"/>
      </media>
      <para id="para-00019">What is the equation for the curve of best fit that models the data?</para>
      <exercise id="_0f36a607-99c7-4403-888f-af72446d761d" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00003">
          <para id="para-00020">Multiple Choice:</para>
          <para id="para-00021"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>6.3</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>8</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>10.6</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para><para id="para-00022"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>3.1</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>2.6</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>7.93</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para><para id="para-00023"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>4.31</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>3.2</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>6.08</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para><para id="para-00024"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>5.1</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>9.2</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>7.14</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para></problem>
        <solution id="sol-00003">
          <para id="para-00025">Try again. Revisit activity 8.12.2.</para>
          <para id="para-00026">The correct answer is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>4.31</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>3.2</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>6.08</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <list class="os-raise-noindent" list-type="enumerated" id="list-00004">
        <item>Enter the given data into Desmos, then calculate the regression approximation to determine the curve of best fit. <table class="unnumbered os-raise-skinnytable" id="table-00004">
            <tgroup cols="2">
              <tbody>
                <row>
                  <entry><emphasis><m:math><m:mrow><m:msub><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>1</m:mn></m:msub></m:mrow></m:math></emphasis>
                  </entry>
                  <entry><emphasis><m:math><m:mrow><m:msub><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mn>1</m:mn></m:msub></m:mrow></m:math></emphasis>
                  </entry>
                </row>
                <row>
                  <entry> 0.3 </entry>
                  <entry> 25 </entry>
                </row>
                <row>
                  <entry> 0.6 </entry>
                  <entry> 36 </entry>
                </row>
                <row>
                  <entry> 1.2 </entry>
                  <entry> 45 </entry>
                </row>
                <row>
                  <entry> 1.8 </entry>
                  <entry> 33 </entry>
                </row>
                <row>
                  <entry> 2.3 </entry>
                  <entry> 12 </entry>
                </row>
              </tbody>
            </tgroup>
          </table>
        </item>
      </list>
      <media alt="...">
        <iframe src="../../media/desmos/73a41d9f6d133fb73de34f9f4ccacd50756a4c9c.html" width="500" height="400"/>
      </media>
      <para id="para-00027">What is the equation for the curve of best fit that models the data?</para>
      <exercise id="_57966c39-30be-48a6-8aeb-6e20d037a229" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00004">
          <para id="para-00028">Multiple Choice:</para>
          <para id="para-00029"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>25.41</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>59.28</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>9.64</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para><para id="para-00030"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>30.84</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>49.61</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>8.99</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para><para id="para-00031"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>3.72</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>7.34</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>8.67</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para><para id="para-00032"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>35.78</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>45.21</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>3.74</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para></problem>
        <solution id="sol-00004">
          <para id="para-00033">Try again. Revisit activities 8.12.2.</para>
          <para id="para-00034">The correct answer is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>25.41</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>59.28</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>9.64</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <para id="para-00035">For questions 5 – 9, use the following information.</para>
      <para id="para-00036"><quote id="quote-00001">The path of a toy rocket after launch is modeled by the following data set. The height of the rocket, in feet, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>, corresponds to the number of seconds passed, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>.</quote></para>
      <media alt="...">
        <iframe src="../../media/desmos/9c35f4a1131f245ab788215077a301fd3447ea4a.html" width="500" height="400"/>
      </media>
      <exercise id="b90b03f7-6d4e-43e9-ab11-78fd7d4711c5" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00005">
          <para id="para-00037">What is the equation for the curve of best fit that models the flight of the toy rocket?</para>
          <para id="para-00038">Multiple Choice:</para>
          <para id="para-00039"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>6.1</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>31</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>1.24</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para><para id="para-00040"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>11.9</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>30.2</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>3.64</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para><para id="para-00041"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>4.2</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>34</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>6.34</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para><para id="para-00042"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>9.2</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>46</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>3.51</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para></problem>
        <solution id="sol-00005">
          <para id="para-00043">Try again. Revisit activity 8.12.3.</para>
          <para id="para-00044">The correct answer is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>9.2</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>46</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>3.51</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="_147dbf86-c93a-48c1-ab7f-05529b149e93" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00006">
          <para id="para-00045">Approximately how high will the rocket be 2 seconds after launch?</para>
          <para id="para-00046">Multiple Choice:</para>
          <para id="para-00047">45.91 feet</para>
          <para id="para-00048">53.60 feet</para>
          <para id="para-00049">58.71 feet</para>
          <para id="para-00050">61.00 feet</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00006">
          <para id="para-00051">Try again. Revisit activities 8.12.3.</para>
          <para id="para-00052">The correct answer is 58.71 feet.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="_436af224-3161-411e-8ab5-eb1def5c2205" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00007">
          <para id="para-00053">At what approximate times after launch will the rocket have a height of 20 feet?</para>
          <para id="para-00054">Multiple Choice:</para>
          <para id="para-00055">0.26 seconds after launch and 4.74 seconds after launch</para>
          <para id="para-00056">0.39 seconds after launch and 4.61 seconds after launch</para>
          <para id="para-00057">0.52 seconds after launch and 4.48 seconds after launch</para>
          <para id="para-00058">0.82 seconds after launch and 4.18 seconds after launch</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00007">
          <para id="para-00059">Try again. Revisit activity 8.12.3.</para>
          <para id="para-00060">The correct answer is 0.39 seconds after launch and 4.61 seconds after launch.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="_16d27a20-3e37-4123-b6d5-1fadbc84bd28" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00008">
          <para id="para-00061">Approximately how long will it take the rocket to reach its maximum height?</para>
          <para id="para-00062">Multiple Choice:</para>
          <para id="para-00063">1.73 seconds</para>
          <para id="para-00064">2.50 seconds</para>
          <para id="para-00065">3.20 seconds</para>
          <para id="para-00066">5.08 seconds</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00008">
          <para id="para-00067">Try again. Revisit activity 8.12.3.</para>
          <para id="para-00068">The correct answer is 2.50 seconds.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="_15839ded-e850-4b5f-8918-5debe5f219e3" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00009">
          <para id="para-00069">Approximately how long will it take for the rocket to land on the ground?</para>
          <para id="para-00070">Multiple Choice:</para>
          <para id="para-00071">2.50 seconds</para>
          <para id="para-00072">4.63 seconds</para>
          <para id="para-00073">5.08 seconds</para>
          <para id="para-00074">6.12 seconds</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00009">
          <para id="para-00075">Try again. Revisit activity 8.12.3.</para>
          <para id="para-00076">The correct answer is 5.08 seconds.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <para id="para-00077">For question 10, Maria has found a curve of best fit using the equation below.</para>
      <media alt="...">
        <iframe src="../../media/desmos/dc8c59067ba553f99987d0ad5b784b8d94eb5657.html" width="500" height="400"/>
      </media>
      <exercise id="_50848151-29ad-4f88-a8a1-521249bd70f8" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00010">
          <para id="para-00078">What is the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-value Maria is asked to predict?</para>
          <para id="para-00079">Maria is asked to predict the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-value on her curve when <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>10</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>. To do this, she graphs the function <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>10</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> and analyzes the intersection point of the curve and the line.</para>
          <para id="para-00080">Multiple Choice:</para>
          <para id="para-00081">10</para>
          <para id="para-00082">93</para>
          <para id="para-00083">105</para>
          <para id="para-00084">111</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00010">
          <para id="para-00085">Try again. Revisit activity 8.12.4.</para>
          <para id="para-00086">The correct answer is 111.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
    </section>
